<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
    <!--
        The foss build declares one permission of its own — CAMERA, for scanning an authenticator
        QR code, asked for at the moment of use. The other two reach its merged manifest from
        androidx.biometric, for the fingerprint unlock the user opts into.
        That set is pinned by the `checkFlavorPermissions` Gradle task — this comment is not the
        guarantee; that task is.

        This used to read "deliberately zero-permission", which was not true of the artifact
        anyone installed: the merged manifest carried POST_NOTIFICATIONS, WAKE_LOCK,
        ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE, RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED, FOREGROUND_SERVICE and the two biometric
        permissions, because one daily backup reminder pulled in androidx.work. That reminder is
        now an in-app banner (StaleExportReminder) and the five WorkManager permissions are gone.

        Never add INTERNET.
    -->

    <!--
        ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE arrives from androidx.media3:media3-common, which CameraX's
        camera-view pulls in for video APIs this app never touches (the scanner uses PreviewView
        and ImageAnalysis). It grants nothing here — there is no INTERNET whose state could matter
        — but an air-gapped build that asks about the network is making a claim it should not, and
        checkFlavorPermissions failed on it the moment the scanner moved into foss. Removed rather
        than allowlisted. The play flavour keeps it: Play Billing genuinely uses it.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE" tools:node="remove" />
</manifest>
